# Review routing. One file per algorithm is what makes this useful: a PR that
# corrects md5-pass-salt touches one small file, and this line is why that PR
# reaches a reviewer who can check it rather than sitting in a queue.
#
# The data layers get different scrutiny on purpose. data/tools/ is generated
# from the canonical binaries and a hand-edit there is almost always a
# mistake; data/algorithms/ is the curated surface a contribution edits.

*                       @roycewilliams

# Generated inventories. Regenerated by the extractors, never hand-edited.
/data/tools/            @roycewilliams

# The curated layer -- the PR surface.
/data/algorithms/       @roycewilliams

# The gate, the schema, and the tools that write data.
/schema/                @roycewilliams
/tools/                 @roycewilliams
/.github/               @roycewilliams
